  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>An ice world with a shallow brine ocean under a crust of only nine kilometres, warmed by tides raised by an uncatalogued companion in a two-to-one resonance. The surface is scored by parallel ridges that run three quarters of the way round the world without deviating by more than a degree. Chemosynthetic material has been recovered from a vent plume without landing, and that recovery is the entire basis of the biological entry.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
